      "key": {
        "uuid": "b1ab829b_c46c4c1e",
        "filename": "tests/unit/java/com/android/server/connectivity/mdns/MdnsAnnouncerTest.kt",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 192,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-13T09:32:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think there\u0027s a good way to do that, IPv4 uses 4 bytes in decimal format (123.0.2.192.in-addr.arpa), while IPv6 uses hexadecimal digits (4 bits each) separated by dots (1.0.0.[...].8.B.D.1.0.0.2.ip6.arpa). So the implementations would be very different, IPv4 should probably be a separate method.\n\nBut for IPv4 it\u0027s actually simpler/more readable to just write \"arrayOf(\"123\", \"0\", \"2\", \"192\", \"in-addr\", \"arpa\")\", so I think a method isn\u0027t really needed",
      "parentUuid": "4e872b5b_42b8778a",
